flpdf -- the FreeLFS document viewer ("Documents")
==================================================

    flpdf [--page N] [--zoom PERCENT] [--find TEXT] [--no-contents] FILE

PDF, XPS, EPUB and CBZ through MuPDF (recipe mupdf: static libraries, no X11/GL
viewer, no CJK fallback fonts). Pages are laid out in one continuous column;
only the pages on screen are drawn, from cached display lists (8 pages), straight
into the window buffer. MuPDF's store is capped at 24 MB. Idle RSS is about 17 MB
for a small PDF.

Keys
  Down, Up, wheel         scroll                 Space, Page Down/Up   one screen
  Home, End               start, end             N / P                 next, previous page
  + / - / Ctrl+wheel      zoom (wheel: at the pointer)
  0                       fit width              9   fit page          1   100 %
  Ctrl+F or /             search                 Enter, F3, Ctrl+G     next match (Shift: previous)
  C or F9                 show or hide Contents  Escape                clear the search, then quit
Mouse: drag pans; a click on a link follows it (internal links jump, a web address
is copied to the clipboard); the page box takes a page number and Enter; clicking an
entry in Contents goes to its page.

Search runs one page at a time as you step through matches, and highlights every
hit on the pages in view. Page sizes are measured on timer ticks after the first
page is up, so a large document opens at once.

Not done: password-protected files (reported, not opened), text selection and copy,
annotations and forms, printing.

Test: make check (python3; no compositor). tests/mkpdf.py writes the PostScript for
the report with bookmarks and links used for the screenshots (ghostscript turns it
into a PDF).
